Leave out of the wasip1 build the commands that cannot run on slicc and
that make gh.wasm too large for a Cloudflare Dynamic Worker.

Reason: a Dynamic Worker's code is at most 64 MiB, and gh.wasm 2.102.0-2
is 78 MB, so slicc-kernel's Cloudflare kernel cannot load it ("Dynamic
Worker code size (78982007 bytes) exceeds the maximum allowed size of
67108864 bytes"). attestation and release verify/verify-asset bring in
sigstore-go, TUF, in-toto and their protobuf (13.6 MB); release/shared
has them through attestation.go, which only verify and verify-asset use.
codespace needs SSH and gRPC (6.6 MB). copilot downloads a native binary,
preview is a demo of the interactive prompts, and send-telemetry is the
child gh starts with os/exec, which wasip1 cannot (3.6 MB together). With
this patch and wasm-opt -Oz, gh.wasm is 49.8 MB.

Upstream: not for upstream (a slicc build choice).
removeWhen: Dynamic Workers take more than 64 MiB of code, or these
commands can run on slicc.

